        "title": "Graph Representations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The representation is not a detail — it *is* the cost model. Every bound in the\nrest of this directory is quoted in terms of V (vertices) and E (edges), and\nwhether a bound is achievable at all depends on whether your representation makes\n\"iterate neighbors of v\" cheap (lists) or \"does edge (u,v) exist?\" cheap\n(matrix). Pick wrong and an O(V+E) algorithm silently becomes O(V²)."
    },
