        "title": "Graph Representations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read this as four encodings of one fact set.** The list and CSR scale with the\n*number of edges*; the matrix scales with the *number of vertex pairs*. For the\nsparse graphs that dominate real systems (E ≈ V, not V²), that difference is the\nwhole game."
